<title>USA: Autozone chairman Hyde retires.</title>
<headline>Autozone chairman Hyde retires.</headline>
<dateline>MEMPHIS, Tenn. 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>AutoZone Inc said on Tuesday that J.R. Hyde III retired as chairman of AutoZone's board of directors.</p>
<p>Hyde remains an active director and major shareholder, with 8.2 percent of the company, Autozone said.</p>
<p>Johnston Adams Jr., previously chief executive officer and president, was elected chairman and chief executive officer, the company said.</p>
<p>Timothy Vargo, previously vice chairman and chief operating officer, was elected president and chief operating officer, the company said.</p>
